  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1121 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nIn the early morning hours on Wednesday, a line of showers\nand thunderstorms associated with the aforementioned cold front\nwill move through Middle TN. The diurnal minimum of instability\nduring FROPA bodes well for our mitigated severe weather\npotential, but PWATs are quite high (almost at the 99th \npercentile), so rain rates will be very heavy overnight. Given the\nforward motion of the front looking fairly progressive, widespread\nflash flooding is not expected. Will need to monitor individual\nstorm motions along the front producing training storms with heavy\nrainfall, but this will be an overall beneficial rainfall for\nMiddle TN. Rainfall should clear the area by midnight Wednesday\nnight. Some patchy fog will be supported behind the front \nThursday morning. \n\nThings cool back off to near normal in the upper 60s behind the \nfront on Thursday as light post-frontal showers linger. We'll \nhave some low-end rain chances (less than 20%) on Saturday, but \nother than that, expect dry and cool conditions through next \nweekend.",
